WEBVTT

00:00.290 --> 00:04.840
When I'm marking practice answers,
the first thing I look for is the overview.

00:05.240 --> 00:06.470
So here's a quick check.

00:07.520 --> 00:10.400
A Task 1 answer has four parts.

00:10.400 --> 00:13.580
An introduction that paraphrases the question.

00:14.280 --> 00:16.360
An overview with the big picture.

00:17.040 --> 00:19.780
Then two body paragraphs with the figures.

00:20.450 --> 00:24.230
Now look at this answer. Where's the overview?

00:26.230 --> 00:29.820
It's here, at the end of the second body paragraph.

00:31.060 --> 00:35.440
The reader has to hunt for it, and it's easy to miss.

00:35.960 --> 00:40.500
Move it up. Make it your second paragraph,
and start it with “Overall”.

00:41.610 --> 00:47.880
That's the structure we practise in this course:
four parts, in the same order, whatever the task.
